      "type": "narrative-update",
      "date": "2026-05-13T09:07:36.000Z",
      "title": "GODREJCP: Upcoming Board Meeting And Interim Dividend Will Support Bullish Outlook",
      "body": "Analysts have trimmed their price target on Godrej Consumer Products from about ₹1,316 to about ₹1,273, citing updated assumptions that combine slightly lower profit margins with higher expected revenue growth and a modestly higher future P/E multiple. What's in the News Board meeting scheduled on May 6, 2026, at 13:30 IST to review audited financial results for the quarter and full year ended March 31, 2026 (company filing) Directors to consider declaration of an interim dividend at the May 6, 2026 board meeting (company filing) Board to consider convening the 26th annual general meeting of shareholders on Friday, August 7, 2026 (company filing) Agenda also includes discussion of other matters relating to the company at the upcoming board meeting (company filing) Valuation Changes Fair Va",
      "keyDevTypeId": null,
      "source_url": "https://simplywall.st/community/narratives/in/household/nse-godrejcp/godrej-consumer-products-shares/pr2ixi0g-godrejcp-upcoming-board-meeting-and-dividend-will-drive-fresh-upside/updates/21-analysts-have-trimmed-their-price-target-on-godrej-consumer",
      "raw_subtype": "narrative-update"
    },
    {
      "id": "d7c2e843-cd89-464e-9c4d-de5619999dc2",
      "type": "brief",
      "date": "2026-05-08T16:58:46.000Z",
      "title": "Fourth quarter dividend of ₹5.00 announced",
      "body": "Dividend of ₹5.00 is the same as last year. Ex-date: 12th May 2026 Payment date: 4th June 2026 Dividend yield will be 1.9%, which is higher than the industry average of 1.4%. Sustainability & Growth Dividend is not covered by earnings (110% earnings payout ratio) nor is it covered by cash flows (107% cash payout ratio). The dividend has increased by an average of 27% per year over the past 10 years. However, payments have been volatile during that time. The company's earnings per share (EPS) would need to grow by 22% to bring the payout ratio under control. EPS is expected to grow by 65% over the next 3 years, which is sufficient to bring the dividend into a sustainable range.",
      "keyDevTypeId": null,
      "source_url": null,
      "raw_subtype": "BriefActivity"
    },
    {
      "id": "cb91b0e7-1df1-4962-b4b6-13616e53f78e",
      "type": "brief",
      "date": "2026-05-07T17:29:42.000Z",
      "title": "Full year 2026 earnings: EPS and revenues miss analyst expectations",
      "body": "Full year 2026 results: EPS: ₹18.19 (up from ₹18.11 in FY 2025). Revenue: ₹154.4b (up 7.5% from FY 2025). Net income: ₹18.6b (flat on FY 2025). Profit margin: 12% (in line with FY 2025). Revenue missed analyst estimates by 2.1%. Earnings per share (EPS) also missed analyst estimates by 11%. Revenue is forecast to grow 9.3% p.a. on average during the next 3 years, compared to a 7.5% growth forecast for the Personal Products industry in India. Over the last 3 years on average, earnings per share has increased by 11% per year but the company’s share price has only increased by 2% per year, which means it is significantly lagging earnings growth.",
      "keyDevTypeId": null,
